        "id": "0b110000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "New patient registration",
        "level": 1,
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0b110000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "Welcome to the practice. This form registers you as a patient, and its health questionnaire tells your new clinicians about your health, so that your first appointment can be about you rather than your paperwork.",
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0b110000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "Filling in this form",
        "level": 2,
        "alignment": "left"
      },
      {
        "id": "0b110000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
        "type": "bullet_list",
        "items": [
          "Fill in one form for each person registering, including each child. A parent or guardian can fill it in for a child under 16.",
          "You do not need proof of address, immigration status or an NHS number to register. If you have an NHS number, it helps us find your records faster.",
          "Answer the health questions as fully as you can. If you are not sure of an answer, leave it and we will ask you at your first appointment.",
          "Bring the form to reception or send it to us using the practice's online registration page."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "0b110000-0000-4000-8000-000000000005",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "text": "How we use your information: we use the information on this form to register you with the NHS, to ask your previous practice to send us your records, and to care for you. We share it with other people and services involved in your care, such as hospitals and community teams, and with NHS bodies where the law requires it. Your records stay with the NHS for as long as NHS records retention rules require. Ask reception for our full privacy notice, which also explains how to opt out of your information being used for research and planning.",
        "runs": [
          {
            "text": "How we use your information:",
            "bold": true
          },
          {
            "text": " we use the information on this form to register you with the NHS, to ask your previous practice to send us your records, and to care for you. We share it with other people and services involved in your care, such as hospitals and community teams, and with NHS bodies where the law requires it. Your records stay with the NHS for as long as NHS records retention rules require. Ask reception for our full privacy notice, which also explains how to opt out of your information being used for research and planning."
          }
        ],
        "alignment": "left"
      },
